If transposing, play the root chord of the transposed (Cadd9) and add the 9th note as necessary.

There's a distinct strumming pattern that goes down, up-down; down, up-down.  I know that doesn't help much but you'll feel it immediately while playing along with the song.

TIP:  For (Cadd9) hold (C) and add pinky to 2nd string/3rd fret.  And for (G4) just bring your index finger down from the 5th string to cover the <c> and then back to (G).
       
 
